<title>USA: Fla citrus benefits from rain, in good condition.</title>
<headline>Fla citrus benefits from rain, in good condition.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Florida Agricultural Statistics Service said nearly all the state's citrus is in good to excellent condition, helped along by rain and mild temperatures for the week ended October 6.</p>
<p>New growth persists on young trees and some new growth has appeared on the medium and older trees. &quot;New crop fruit is making good progress but maturity is behind last year at the same time,&quot; FASS said.</p>
<p>FASS also noted some color break on many of the early varieties.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
